  <h2 id={h['sources-and-further-reading'].id}>{h['sources-and-further-reading'].text}</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Amazon SQS, <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/standard-queues.html">Standard queues</a> and <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-visibility-timeout.html">Visibility timeout</a>: at-least-once delivery, possible reordering, and what happens to a message that is not deleted in time.</li>
    <li>RabbitMQ, <a href="https://www.rabbitmq.com/docs/confirms">Consumer acknowledgements and publisher confirms</a>: requeuing of unacknowledged deliveries and what a publisher’s confirmation means.</li>
    <li>Apache Kafka, <a href="https://kafka.apache.org/intro">Introduction</a>: keys, partitions and the order in which a consumer reads a partition.</li>
    <li>Stripe, <a href="https://docs.stripe.com/webhooks">Receive Stripe events in your webhook endpoint</a>: retries, duplicate events, no ordering promise, and why to answer before doing the work. One provider’s behaviour, useful as a model of what to look for in another’s.</li>
    <li>Postmark, <a href="https://postmarkapp.com/developer/webhooks/bounce-webhook">Bounce webhook</a>: a callback that carries the original message id.</li>
    <li>Chris Richardson, <a href="https://microservices.io/patterns/data/saga.html">Pattern: Saga</a>, and the Azure Architecture Center’s <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/patterns/compensating-transaction">Compensating Transaction pattern</a>: orchestration and choreography, compensation that can fail, and points of no return.</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.asyncapi.com/docs/concepts">AsyncAPI concepts</a>: a specification for describing event-driven interfaces as channels and messages, for when the flow in the diagram also needs a written contract.</li>
    <li>Mermaid, <a href="https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/sequenceDiagram.html">Sequence diagrams</a>: the arrows, notes, <code>par</code> and <code>alt</code> used in the listings above.</li>
